   {
    "name": "ambulance_agreement.txt",
    "text": "Sentinel Ambulance Service\nBookings Office\n\n2027-02-18\n\nDear Daniel Mwangi,\n\nThank you for your booking and payment. This letter is your agreement with us for ambulance cover at the Cathedral School Charity Run 5K on 2027-05-01. One ambulance and two paramedics will be on site at the top of Ash Avenue, in place by 07:15, and will stay until the race has finished. Booking reference EV-67693.\n\nOur crew leader will find your race director when they arrive.\n\nKind regards,\nPriya Raman\nBookings Manager\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "CERTIFICATE OF LIABILITY INSURANCE\nCertificate no. AG-80964\nIssued: February 18, 2027\n\nINSURER: Meridian Mutual Insurance\nPOLICY NUMBER: EL-856729\n\nNAMED INSURED: Cathedral School Parents' Group\nDESCRIPTION OF OPERATIONS: Public liability for a foot race, the Cathedral School Charity Run 5K\nVENUE: Clocktower Square, Port Halden\n\nPOLICY PERIOD\nEffective: April 30, 2027\nExpiry: May 2, 2027\n\nLIMIT OF LIABILITY: $1,000,000 each occurrence\n\nThis certificate is issued for information only and confers no rights upon the holder beyond those of the policy.\n\nCertificate holder: City of Port Halden, Events Office\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Medical cover for the Cathedral School Charity Run 5K, Saturday 1 May 2027\n\nFrom Daniel Mwangi, Club Chair, Cathedral School Parents' Group\n\nThe race is a 5K with 50 runners and starts at 08:30. On-site ambulance cover is set out in the attached paperwork from Sentinel Ambulance Service.\n\nFirst aid\nWe'll have 3 first aid posts, at the start, the finish and halfway, with 10 trained first aiders between them, so nobody on the course is more than about a kilometre and a half from help. We also have two first aiders on bikes, carrying defibrillators.\n\nHeat, cold and water\nThere's water every 2.5 km. We look at the forecast two days before and again two hours before. Over 28 degrees we start earlier or cut the course, and over 32 degrees we call it off. If it's cold or wet, we have foil blankets and a warm tent at the finish.\n\nIf someone needs hospital\nThe nearest emergency department is at Port Halden General Hospital, 3 km from the finish. We've walked the route out from the pick-up point at the top of Ash Avenue with the first aiders, and we've told the hospital the date and how many are coming.\n\nStaying in touch\nEveryone at a post and both bike first aiders has a radio on our medical channel, with phones as backup. Calls for an ambulance go through our medical lead, who tells the crew which barrier to come to.\n\nWho's responsible\nOur medical lead is Carl Jensen, a registered paramedic, who'll be there from an hour before the start until the last runner is in and has the final word on pulling any runner out.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "Cathedral School Charity Run 5K - race notes\nCathedral School Parents' Group / contact Daniel Mwangi 555-0197\nSaturday 1 May 2027, gun 08:30, course closes 09:45\n5K (5k), approx 50 entered\n\nROUTE\nAsh Avenue, Orchard Road, Canon Road and Quay Street. all closed. major x-ings: High Street, Queen's Road, Prince Street and Regent Road. finish the Civic Plaza\n\nWIDTHS\nAsh Avenue 16m kerb to kerb. Canon Road 10m. Quay Street 16m. pavements extra. start pens side by side across full road\n\nOTHER\nnumbers from the top of Ash Avenue 1hr before. chip timing. water on course. results online same day\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "traffic_plan.txt",
    "text": "TRAFFIC MANAGEMENT PLAN\nEvent: Cathedral School Charity Run 5K\nDate: Saturday 1 May 2027\nApplicant: Cathedral School Parents' Group\nPrepared by: Halloway Road Management\nIssue: 1.3\n\n1. Scope\nThis plan describes how traffic will be managed for the Cathedral School Charity Run 5K, a 5K race in the Clocktower Square area of Port Halden with a 08:30 start. It has been prepared to accompany the permit application and should be read with the race plan. Police attendance has been requested, but we have not had an answer yet.\n\n2. Road closures\nTemporary closures will be in force as follows, with barriers and advance signing supplied by Signal Hill Traffic Services.\n- Ash Avenue, Weir Street to Castle Way: closed 07:15 to 10:15\n- Orchard Road, Rope Walk to Garrison Street: closed 07:15 to 10:15\n- Canon Road, Weir Street to Castle Way: closed 07:15 to 10:15\n- Quay Street, Garrison Street to Weir Street: closed 07:15 to 10:15\n\n3. Major crossings\nBusier junctions along the course will receive appropriate supervision during the event. Staffing levels will be determined by Signal Hill Traffic Services on the morning, taking account of conditions at the time, with resources deployed flexibly to where they are most needed.\n\n4. Diversions\nDrivers will be advised to expect delays in the area and to allow additional time for their journeys. Advance information boards will be used where practical, and through traffic is expected to find alternative routes across the wider network.\n\n5. Emergency vehicle access\nA clear lane of at least 3.5 m will be kept along the closed section for emergency vehicles. Barrier staff hold radios on the event channel and can open any closure within two minutes on request from the event controller, who is in direct contact with the police and ambulance control rooms.\n\n6. Notification\nDetails of the event will be published on the organiser's website and shared through social media in the weeks leading up to race day.\n\n7. Reopening\nA sweep vehicle follows the last runner. Closures are lifted in the order listed, after a barrier and litter check, with all roads open by 10:15.\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "Hello,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nHere is our application for the Cathedral School Charity Run 5K, Saturday 1 May 2027. 50 runners, 5K, off at 08:30, around Clocktower Square. I've attached ambulance_agreement.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, race_plan.txt, traffic_plan.txt.\n\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\n\nThanks,\nDaniel\n\nDaniel Mwangi, Cathedral School Parents' Group\n555-0197\n",
